From d35d46d3bbc123166364617e03ac009cff8b7e6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:22:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 43/45] decide: cell budget bounded by the SWA cache

On a model with sliding-window attention layers the context has a second, smaller KV cache (src/llama-kv-cache-iswa.cpp:73). Every cell limit of the engine is now min(n_ctx, SWA cells) - 16, so a state over the SWA cache gets 400 budget naming it and --swa-full instead of a 500 (spec 5.3 rev 5). engine_config gains swa_full; info reports memory.swa_cells for such models.
